Z||000000||burdell1||10-01-1999||01:05 PM||||I read awhile back on the forum that someone brought their aluminum wheels someplace to be refinished and that it only cost them $20 per wheel. I thought I would that too, but I found out around here it is more like $135 per wheel. So, I'm debating whether or not I should try to do it myself (which seems a lot easier said than done) or get a used set of rims and get hubcaps instead. What do you guys think? Since I'm still trying to pay off my repairs from the other times I've gotten my Fiero fixed, money is an issue. Also, I'm trying to save my money so I can buy a different car (so I won't have to drive my Fiero in the harsh MN winters.)<BR>||||reg||5
